* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13g2-lock-detector-window (issue #81, Part of #16 via #78)
* ONE phase-error ladder point (copy A discharged-start + copy B
* charged-start) -- see ../testbench/tb_lock_recovery.sp.tmpl's header for why
* the ladder is split into one small independent ngspice invocation per point
* rather than one large merged deck.
*
* Carried over (topology, not device-specific) from
* ../../sg13cmos5l-lock-detector-window/testbench/tb_lock_ladder_point.sp.tmpl
* (issue #52). ../testbench/gen_ladder.py's `gen --fracs-set <set>
* --only-index <k>` fills in @LADDER_DEVICES@ / @LADDER_IC@ / @LADDER_MEAS@ /
* @LADDER_SAVE@ exactly the way it does for the SG13CMOS5L sibling.
*
* Placeholders (substituted by ../testbench/run.sh via gen_ladder.py, not
* meant to be run directly): @CORNER_MOS@, @CORNER_RES@, @CORNER_CAP@,
* @TEMP@, @VSUP@, @VMID@, @TREF@, @TRST@, @TSTEP@, @TSTOP@, @TSETTLE@, @DUT@,
* @LADDER_DEVICES@, @LADDER_IC@, @LADDER_MEAS@, @LADDER_SAVE@.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerCAP.lib @CORNER_CAP@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include @DUT@

.param vsup=@VSUP@
.param tref=@TREF@
.param trst=@TRST@
.param ttr=100p
.param ttd='tref'

Vsub sub! 0 0
Vdd vdd 0 dc @VSUP@

* ---- phase-error ladder point: copy A (discharged start) + copy B (charged) --
@LADDER_DEVICES@

@LADDER_IC@

* SOLVER-EFFORT NOTE -- itl4=5000 gmin=1e-11, reused verbatim from the
* SG13CMOS5L sibling (issue #66, Part of #16) per issue #81's own Scope item
* 1. Neither is an accuracy relaxation: reltol/abstol/vntol/chgtol are
* untouched. Both are needed for the same topology-level reason on THIS PDK:
* nand2_hv's own series-stack internal node `mid1` has no DC path to either
* rail whenever both stacked NMOS are off (gmin is exactly what that floating
* node needs), and the high-impedance integrating node (driven only by
* XRPU's weak pull-up and XMPD's pull-down) can sit at intermediate voltages
* for the whole run, which is where ngspice's default Newton-iteration budget
* gives out (itl4). Both cells (nand2_hv, and the XRPU/XMPD/XCW integrator)
* are identical topology on both PDKs -- only the device models differ -- so
* the same solver settings apply here even though this PDK's block has not
* yet had the SG13CMOS5L XMPD re-size (issue #66) applied to it.
.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-10 vntol=1e-5 chgtol=1e-13 itl4=5000 gmin=1e-11
.tran @TSTEP@ @TSTOP@

.control
@LADDER_SAVE@
run
@LADDER_MEAS@
.endc
.end
